<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3540" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκρο-βυστία</span></b> , ἡ,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>foreskin</i>, <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Ge.</u>
				17.11
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				49
			</span></i> H., <i><span class="en">
				<u>Act.Ap.</u>
				11.3
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>state of having the foreskin, uncircumcision,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ep.Rom.
				2.25
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> collect.,
				<i>the uncircumcised</i>, ib.<i><span class="en">
				2.26
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				3.30
			</span></i>, etc. (Prob. from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄκρος</span>
			and a Semitic root, cf. Bab. <i>buśtu</i> 'pudenda',
			Heb. <i>bōsheth</i> 'shame': wrongly derived from
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄκρος, βύω</span> by <i><span class="en">
				<u>EM</u>
				53.48
			</span></i>.)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
